Subject: [freebsd-ports PATCH 2/2] net-mgmt/signoz: Name the collector's port
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:22:28 +0000

SigNoz cannot run without the SigNoz OpenTelemetry Collector, which
creates the ClickHouse schema and ingests the telemetry. The package
text only said the collector was packaged separately, leaving users to
find it. It now names net-mgmt/signoz-otel-collector. The collector is
not a dependency, since it may run on another host.
---
 net-mgmt/signoz/files/pkg-message.in | 4 ++--
 net-mgmt/signoz/pkg-descr            | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/net-mgmt/signoz/files/pkg-message.in b/net-mgmt/signoz/files/pkg-message.in
index e0acc0c39ab4..7df9f7db4d69 100644
--- a/net-mgmt/signoz/files/pkg-message.in
+++ b/net-mgmt/signoz/files/pkg-message.in
@@ -4,8 +4,8 @@
 SigNoz stores telemetry in ClickHouse (databases/clickhouse), which may
 run on another host. Before the first start, ClickHouse needs a cluster
 named "cluster" and the SigNoz schema. The schema is created by the
-schema migrator of the SigNoz OpenTelemetry Collector, which also
-ingests the telemetry and is packaged separately.
+SigNoz OpenTelemetry Collector (net-mgmt/signoz-otel-collector), which
+also ingests the telemetry and may run on another host.
 
 Settings come from built-in defaults, from %%ETCDIR%%/signoz.yaml,
 and from SIGNOZ_* variables set in signoz_env, each overriding the one
diff --git a/net-mgmt/signoz/pkg-descr b/net-mgmt/signoz/pkg-descr
index 951ff383d910..66a9c0461702 100644
--- a/net-mgmt/signoz/pkg-descr
+++ b/net-mgmt/signoz/pkg-descr
@@ -5,4 +5,4 @@ stores its data in ClickHouse.
 
 This is the Community Edition of the query service and web interface.
 Telemetry reaches ClickHouse through the SigNoz distribution of the
-OpenTelemetry Collector, which is packaged separately.
+OpenTelemetry Collector, net-mgmt/signoz-otel-collector.
